    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44627" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐόργ-ητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>good-tempered</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. πρὸς τὸ πρέπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gorg.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς κόλαξι . . εὐόργητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					25
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὐ. καὶ πρᾶον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>MM</u>
					1186a23
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.413c
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, προσομιλεῖν τῷ πολέμῳ</span>
			<i>with good temper</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργισθείς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.122
			</span></i>.</div>
